The  driver supports the following Microchip I/O Expanders: 8‐bit
I/O expander, I2C interface 8‐bit  I/O  expander,  SPI  interface
16‐bit  I/O  expander, I2C interface 16‐bit I/O expander, SPI in‐
terface 16‐bit I/O expander, open‐drain  outputs,  I2C  interface
16‐bit  I/O expander, open‐drain outputs, SPI interface Access to
the pins is provided by the interface.  The SPI version of  these
devices  support  multiple  chips per chip select signal.  On the
MCP23S08 and MCP23S17, this is achieved by tying the address  se‐
lect  pins  to VDD or GND to select an address The MCP23S18 has a
similar capability, but uses an analog voltage input on a  single
address select pin, along with an internal voltage divider ladder
and  a  series of comparators to generate the 3 address bits; see
the data sheet for details.  The argument  in  the  configuration
directive for SPI attachments selects the hardware address of the
chip  instance  for  that  driver instance.  The driver first ap‐
peared in It was overhauled in to support additional  chip  types
and to add the I2C attachment.  The driver was written by and SPI
instances  of  the driver do not utilize the Device Tree bindings
for this device.  The driver does not currently  act  as  a  GPIO
provider for the platform device tree.
